WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.069
Welcome back to State of the Union.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.771
This Friday is the two year

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:07.407
anniversary of the January 6th attacks.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:09.609
The events of that day led to criminal

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:10.744
prosecute actions

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:12.045
and played a role,

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.247
pretty big one in the midterm elections.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.383
They also changed the careers of two

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:17.617
House Republicans

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:18.718
who chose to serve

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:20.020
on the January six committee

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:20.587
and largely

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.922
as a result of that patriotic service.

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:26.259
They both are now leaving Congress.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:28.228
Joining me now is the outgoing

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.596
Republican congressman

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:31.364
of Illinois, Adam Kinzinger.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.166
Thank you so much for joining me.

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:34.634
I really appreciate it.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:35.602
Let's start with the work

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:37.370
that you've been doing over the past

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.238
almost two years,

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:39.572
the January six committee.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.141
It's over

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:41.975
and it's

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:42.742
now in the hands

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:43.910
of the Justice Department.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.645
Do you think that President Trump

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:48.148
ultimately will be charged for crime?

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:50.650
Look, I mean, when I got into this,

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:51.951
when we started this process,

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.186
I didn't know, you know,

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.154
I'm not a lawyer,

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:55.555
not a Justice Department guy,

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.057
didn't necessarily know

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:58.491
is he guilty of a crime or not?

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.160
Obviously, what he did

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.561
from a presidential perspective,

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.763
from an oath perspective as a problem

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.165
as we've gotten into this.

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.199
I look and I'm like, yeah,

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.134
if this is not a crime,

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.069
I don't know what is.

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.437
If if a president

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:12.005
can incite an insurrection

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:13.740
and not be held accountable,

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:14.707
then really there's

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.309
no limit to what a president can do

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.277
or can't do.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:19.312
And so, yeah, I do think

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:20.980
ultimately when we get to

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:21.815
where we're going to go,

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:23.583
I think the Justice Department

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:24.818
will do the right thing.

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.686
I think he will be charged.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:27.854
And I frankly think he should be.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:28.088
I mean,

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:29.622
everything we've uncovered

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:30.924
from what he did

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.092
with the Justice Department

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:32.826
to everything

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.294
leading up to January six

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:36.329
to on January six,

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.565
sitting there for 180 minutes

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:40.567
and watching this occur

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:43.169
in the hope that maybe, just maybe,

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.104
that last attempt

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.271
to stay in power will work.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.407
So he should be charged and convicted.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:48.842
So that's my personal opinion.

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.243
It's not from a

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:50.910
from a lawyer

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.645
just what you've been collecting. Yes.

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.180
And it appears like I look at that

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.082
and I go, if he is not guilty of a crime,

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.618
then I frankly fear

00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:58.785
for the

00:01:58.785 --> 00:01:59.619
future of this country,

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:00.553
because now

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.188
every future president can say,

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:02.689
hey, here's

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:03.556
the bar

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.091
and the bar is

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.526
do everything you can to stay in power.

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.862
You talk about the future of this country

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:11.664
as you are

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:12.499
on your way out

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:14.267
and leaving Congress behind.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.869
Are you optimistic

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:18.271
or fearful for American democracy?

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.406
Well, that's a tough question.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.909
So typically, I'm always optimistic.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:23.510
I try to be

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.612
you can't do this job if you're not.

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:27.480
I'm a little fearful in the short term.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.114
You know,

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:29.282
we are in a moment

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:31.618
where facts don't really matter.

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:32.752
What matters to people

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:33.720
is just what

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:34.587
your opinion is

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:35.221
and the facts

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.557
that that comport to that matter.

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:38.057
We're in a

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:38.892
we're in a moment

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:39.759
where about half

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.127
the country believes there

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.662
that the election was stolen.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.297
Maybe a third of the country now believes

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.832
the election was stolen.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.066
But if you're in a democracy,

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:47.600
and you believe

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:48.735
that your vote doesn't count,

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:50.036
that's dangerous.

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:50.770
So in the short term,

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.472
I'm a little pessimistic,

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.541
but I am in the long term,

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:56.009
very optimistic for this country

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:57.810
because I look back at trends

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.579
I look back at rough times

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:00.613
we have been in

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:01.681
and we've always come out

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.782
and we haven't just come out of them.

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:03.983
We've come out stronger.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:07.187
Democracies are not defined by bad days.

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:08.121
We're defined by

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:10.323
how we come out of those bad days.

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.292
And so in the long term, I am optimistic.

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:13.960
But I got to say to people,

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.162
this is not a moment to rest.

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:17.063
This is a moment

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:18.498
where you have to understand

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.766
there have to be uncomfortable

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:22.902
alliances to defend democracy.

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:23.736
But we can do this.

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:25.538
If you had a Wayback Machine

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.407
and could go back a couple of years

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:29.776
and tell the Congressman Adam

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:31.277
Kinzinger of

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:32.912
I don't know what the

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.948
just the 2020 election,

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:36.282
what you would be doing

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.318
for the two years following

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:39.719
would you say yeah go for it.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.454
Would you have done anything differently.

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:41.854
You know,

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.089
it's a great question

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:45.725
because I get asked a lot like you know

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:46.826
would you have done it differently.

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:48.061
Obviously there's

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:50.363
been some sacrifice and everything in it.

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:52.532
I wouldn't do one thing differently.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.133
Look, I

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.034
you know

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:55.835
the way

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:56.936
this is kind of gone

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:57.904
in the last couple of years.

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.105
It's been tough, right.

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:00.306
You know, I've had

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.674
an extended family

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:02.575
that sent me letters

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:02.976
telling me

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:04.677
that was working on behalf of Satan.

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:05.545
I mean, that's not something

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:06.813
I could have imagined.

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:08.381
Have your family say there.

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:08.815
Yeah.

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:10.283
I mean, it's

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:11.484
nothing I could have imagined,

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:13.319
you know, a couple of years ago.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.654
But what that does to me is it

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:15.622
reminds me of

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:18.424
just how bad of a place we've gotten to.

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:21.327
And, you know, everybody in their life.

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:22.729
And I was no different

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:24.297
when I was a young guy.

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:24.564
You know,

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:25.999
you always imagine

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:28.134
a moment where you can stand alone

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:30.403
and where you're like the one person that

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:32.472
that can do the right thing in a crowd.

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:34.140
Right. Everybody imagines this moment.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:34.907
Very few people

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:37.243
get a chance to actually do that.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:38.378
And I've learned in this job

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:39.512
that very few of those

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:41.281
that get the chance actually do it.

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:44.350
I feel honored to have

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.819
been at this moment in history

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.721
and to have done the right thing.

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:48.988
You know,

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.423
my kids are going to be proud of it.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:50.990
That's something

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.825
that I take very seriously.

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:56.396
And now I want to do anything different

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:57.563
when Congress is sworn in.

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.065
And two days.

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:01.034
You're getting a little emotional.

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:02.402
Just a little. Yeah.

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:04.470
This is tough for you. Yeah.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.306
I think it's it's

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.875
so I'm not going to miss the job.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.577
I'm glad I'm not going to be back.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:12.812
It gives me time to focus on

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:14.947
broader things. Bigger fights.

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:17.517
But it is like,

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:19.185
you know, thinking of Adam Kinzinger

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:21.721
when he's 32 kind of the new freshman,

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:23.823
you know,

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.858
kind of like optimistic and bright eyed

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:27.760
to where we are today.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.495
It's it's an emotional thing

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.431
because it's 12 years of my life. Right.

00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:34.667
And you know I got into this single now

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.169
I'm married with a kid

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:38.071
so I can think about that legacy.

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:40.773
It's been a heck of a ride.

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:41.507
Sure has.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:42.241
I was going to ask

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:43.509
if you are going to be sad

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:45.345
not to be part of the next Congress

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:46.379
in a couple of days.

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:48.614
No, I won't.

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:49.782
Look, I

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:50.850
you know, it's

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:51.284
I want to

00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:53.119
still be able to have an opinion right.

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:54.253
So that's going to be tough is,

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:55.621
I think, adjusting to the fact

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:56.789
that people

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:58.224
will have less interest

00:05:58.224 --> 00:06:00.293
in what you have to say.

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:02.362
But it's a tough time

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:03.296
in Congress right now.

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:03.563
I mean,

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:04.464
it is

00:06:04.764 --> 00:06:06.032
I'm looking at what

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:07.400
this is shaping out to be.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.468
And I know the tough things

00:06:08.468 --> 00:06:11.070
we have gone through in the past.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.705
This is going to be a really tough year.

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:13.406
What does it say

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:15.174
about the future of your party,

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:16.209
the Republican Party,

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:18.077
that Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:20.146
and people like her are kind of ascendant

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:21.881
and the Adam Kinzinger and Liz

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:23.783
Cheney's of the world are

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:25.585
no longer in the in the Congress.

00:06:25.585 --> 00:06:27.019
I think it says to me

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:28.054
that the Republican Party

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:29.689
is not the future of this country

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:31.758
unless it corrects. Right.

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:33.326
Unless there's a change.

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:35.194
Because I got to tell you,

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:37.864
if you think of a successful America

00:06:37.864 --> 00:06:39.165
in 20 years,

00:06:39.165 --> 00:06:40.233
that's not going to be an America

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:41.768
based on what Marjorie

00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:43.002
Taylor Greene wants

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:43.736
or based on what

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:45.605
some of these radicals want.

00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:47.407
The only way this country can succeed

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:49.108
is if we learn to work together.

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:50.643
We once called Kevin McCarthy

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:52.211
a true friend. Yeah.

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:53.679
If you could sit him down.

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.114
Just the two of you right now,

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:56.549
what would you say?

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:58.651
I just let him know I'm disappointed.

00:06:58.651 --> 00:06:58.885
Right.

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:01.521
I mean, he has he as a leader,

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:03.356
not just a member of Congress,

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:05.425
as a leader of Congress,

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:06.826
he had an opportunity

00:07:06.826 --> 00:07:08.594
to tell the truth, the American people.

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:10.129
And he went to Mar a Lago

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:12.198
a couple of weeks after January six

00:07:12.198 --> 00:07:13.533
and resurrected Donald Trump.

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:14.867
He is the reason Donald

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:16.302
Trump is still a factor.

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:17.670
He is the reason that

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:20.106
some of the crazy elements

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:21.207
of the House still exist.

00:07:21.207 --> 00:07:22.141
If he didn't go down there.

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:24.177
You think Trump would have a nice out?

00:07:24.177 --> 00:07:25.311
I do. I do.

00:07:25.311 --> 00:07:26.813
I think I think, first off,

00:07:26.813 --> 00:07:28.414
how do we actually remove

00:07:28.414 --> 00:07:30.049
Trump from office during impeachment?

00:07:30.049 --> 00:07:30.883
That would have been huge.

00:07:30.883 --> 00:07:32.251
Right so that's on McConnell

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:33.419
and some of the Republicans

00:07:33.419 --> 00:07:34.320
in the Senate.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:34.687
But yeah,

00:07:34.687 --> 00:07:36.422
I think the second because I lived it

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:37.623
the second

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:40.359
Kevin McCarthy went to Mar a Lago,

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:42.695
the conference split from like quiet.

00:07:42.728 --> 00:07:43.496
What are we going to do?

00:07:43.496 --> 00:07:45.331
Where are we going to go to?

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:46.599
Begrudgingly defending

00:07:46.599 --> 00:07:47.433
Donald Trump again.

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:48.901
He is responsible, actually.

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:49.602
Donald Trump

00:07:49.602 --> 00:07:51.003
should consider Kevin McCarthy

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:51.871
his best friend

00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:53.439
because Donald Trump is alive

00:07:53.439 --> 00:07:54.240
today politically

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.008
because of Kevin McCarthy.

00:07:56.008 --> 00:07:56.442
Last year

00:07:56.442 --> 00:07:57.543
you told the Huffington Post

00:07:57.543 --> 00:07:58.878
you would love to go up against

00:07:58.878 --> 00:08:01.214
Trump in the 2024 primary

00:08:01.214 --> 00:08:03.416
You said, quote, I think it'd be fun.

00:08:03.416 --> 00:08:04.350
It would be fun.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:05.184
Are you going to run for president?

00:08:05.184 --> 00:08:06.819
No, that's not my intention. No.

00:08:06.819 --> 00:08:08.488
But it would be fun to run against him

00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:11.557
because he stands up and just lies.

00:08:12.258 --> 00:08:14.393
He tells untruths.

00:08:14.393 --> 00:08:16.429
People love it because it's entertaining.

00:08:16.429 --> 00:08:17.563
But eventually

00:08:17.563 --> 00:08:19.232
people have a concern for their country.

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:19.632
So, no,

00:08:19.632 --> 00:08:21.501
my intention is not to run in 2024,

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:24.003
but it would be fun.

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:24.437
It would

00:08:24.437 --> 00:08:24.871
be fun

00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:26.539
to stand on a stage with Donald Trump

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:29.208
and actually tell the truth, because

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:30.776
when he's on a stage, it's

00:08:30.776 --> 00:08:32.812
nothing but lies that come out.

00:08:32.812 --> 00:08:33.346
Well,

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:34.413
no matter what you do,

00:08:34.413 --> 00:08:36.749
I don't think that this is the last

00:08:36.782 --> 00:08:37.149
that we're here.

00:08:37.149 --> 00:08:37.750
If we're going to hear

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:38.751
from Adam Kinzinger,

00:08:38.751 --> 00:08:40.653
thank you so much and thank you

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:41.487
for your service.

00:08:41.487 --> 00:08:43.589
You're obviously also in the

00:08:43.823 --> 00:08:44.657
in the military.

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:45.625
So thank you for that

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:46.359
and everything

00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:47.693
that you've done in Congress as well.

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:48.494
You bet. Thank you.

